course: dictionary
lesson: 10566
title: Uncomfortable: body, feelings and warnings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Uncomfortable has two main meanings. The first is about your body: a hard chair or tight shoes can be uncomfortable. «Babies cry to tell us they are hungry, tired or uncomfortable, because they cannot talk.» Here it means not feeling physically well or at ease.
explain: The second meaning is about feelings. When you feel a bit worried, embarrassed or uneasy, you feel uncomfortable. «A secret that makes you feel worried or uncomfortable should be told to a trusted adult.» Here the word is a warning sign, not just a sore or tight feeling.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a word you know. In «Only video call people you know, and tell an adult if anyone online makes you uncomfortable», you could say uneasy instead, and the sentence still makes sense. So uncomfortable means uneasy here, and you should tell a trusted adult.
fact: Uncomfortable means not nice for your body, like a hard chair or tight shoes.
fact: Uncomfortable also means a bit worried, embarrassed or uneasy.
fact: A situation is uncomfortable when it makes people feel awkward, as in «an uncomfortable silence».
fact: Uncomfortable is an adjective, and its comparative forms are more uncomfortable and most uncomfortable.
fact: If someone makes you feel uncomfortable, you can say no, leave, and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «The hard wooden chair made Sam feel uncomfortable after an hour.» What does uncomfortable mean here? | Cold and wet | *Not nice for your body | Very happy and relaxed | Very loud
exercise: «The room went quiet, and it was an uncomfortable silence.» What does an uncomfortable silence mean? | A silence where everyone is laughing | A silence that is very peaceful and calm | A quiet break in a game | *A silence that makes people feel awkward
exercise: «Tell an adult if anyone online makes you uncomfortable.» What should you do if someone online makes you feel uncomfortable? | Keep it secret and say nothing | Share your password with them | *Say no, leave, and tell a trusted adult | Send more messages to be polite
test: «Babies cry to tell us they are hungry, tired or uncomfortable.» In this sentence, uncomfortable means? | *Not feeling well or at ease | Very rich and full | Happy and singing | Brightly lit
test: Which is the most uncomfortable thing to sit on for a long time? | A warm sofa | A soft cushion | *A hard stone bench | A feather bed
exam: Choose the right word: The bench is ___ than the sofa. | most uncomfortable | uncomfortablest | uncomfortabler | *more uncomfortable
